"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The surgical findings indicate a Gleason 4+4 (ISUP grade group 3) and positive surgical margins, which are concerning features. Counterbalancing these are the absence of extraprostatic extension and no lymph node metastasis documented. The seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymphovascular invasion was present. The nodal status is documented as no lymph node metastasis. The difference between the biopsy and prostatectomy findings is noted, as the biopsy Gleason pattern and ISUP report are missing.\n\nThe uncertainty in the prognosis is heightened by the missing postoperative PSA and any subsequent follow-up data, which are not documented. Information regarding the postoperative PSA and its trajectory would significantly revise this assessment. The current heuristic sensitivity range suggests a horizon for recurrence within a specific interval. The fixed estimated horizon is 51.41 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 41.13–61.69 months; its coverage has not been validated."
